return {
["22:00"]={"At \003ten o’clock\004, he went to Shinjuku and bought a Fujitsu word processor with his credit card. It was the latest model, far lighter than earlier versions.","1Q84, Book One","Haruki Murakami"},
["22:01"]={"At \003one minute past ten\004, Giles shook the last hand and, desperate for a drink, walked down the road to join the dock workers in the Lord Nelson.","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:02"]={"It was now \00310:02 pm\004. He has less than two hours.","The Lost Symbol","Dan Brown"},
["22:03"]={"At \00310:03 pm\004 the ushers pull open the doors and I watch the now-familiar footage of the audience surging into the night, noticeably excited.","The Dark Lake","Sarah Bailey"},
["22:04"]={"On Saturday, November 12, 1955, the Hill Valley Courthouse’s clock tower was struck by lightning, which poured 1.21 gigawatts of energy into the structure. Time stood still at \00310:04\004 on the clock’s face from that day on.","Back to the Future: Race Through Time","Marc Sumerak"},
["22:05"]={"If you do not tell me everything I need to know by—he looked at the watch on his wrist—“by \003ten-oh-five\004 tomorrow night, you will be executed. You and the three exnays.”","Among the Betrayed","Margaret Peterson Haddix"},
["22:06"]={"Let me know as soon as you hear anything.\nQuoyle shivered in the chilly kitchen. The clock said \003six minutes past ten\004. He could not hear the sea.","The Shipping News","E. Annie Proulx"},
["22:07"]={"“Follow the diversion sign,” he said, without even looking at her.\nShe glanced at the clock on her dashboard. It was \00310:07\004.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:08"]={"My watch is always a little fast, I said. “What time do you make it now?”\n“\003Ten eight\004.”\n“Ten eighteen by mine. You see.”","The Quiet American","Graham Greene"},
["22:09"]={"The hour was \003nine minutes past ten\004. My teeth began to chatter of sheer excitement.","Jonah and Co.","Dornford Yates"},
["22:10"]={"At about ten o’clock the first tiny snowflakes came loitering down and settled on Jill’s arm. \003Ten minutes later\004 they were falling quite thickly. In twenty minutes the ground was noticeably white.","The Silver Chair","C.S. Lewis"},
["22:11"]={"Therefore a sergeant called Trifonov had been on post all day or all week and then he had left at \003eleven minutes past ten\004 in the evening.","The Enemy","Lee Child"},
["22:12"]={"The phone rang at \003twelve minutes past ten\004. He grabbed the receiver, and immediately recognized the voice of the local party chairman. “Good evening, Peter.”","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:13"]={"It’s \003ten-thirteen\004, announced Clancy. “In two more minutes—”\n“Post time,” I said.","The Anthem Sprinters","Ray Bradbury"},
["22:14"]={"The shopping bags looked heavy and impressive, their weight making the Chinese women lean in slightly towards each other. Call it \0032214:10h\004.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["22:15"]={"Aargh. Is \00310:15\004. Newsnight in 15 minutes.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["22:16"]={"Nevertheless, when you left me a message, at \00322:16\004 according to Telenor — in other words as soon as you had got in the door — you were obviously pretty excited that you were on the track of something.","The Redbreast","Jo Nesbø"},
["22:17"]={"\00310:17 p.m.\004 Cassette will not go in.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["22:18"]={"My watch is always a little fast, I said. “What time do you make it now?”\n“Ten eight.”\n“\003Ten eighteen\004 by mine. You see.”","The Quiet American","Graham Greene"},
["22:19"]={"\00322:19 GMT\004\nJackie decided that this was even worse than a stakeout, because they were waiting for someone who wasn’t there, rather than for someone who was there and must eventually show up.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:20"]={"At about ten o’clock the first tiny snowflakes came loitering down and settled on Jill’s arm. Ten minutes later they were falling quite thickly. \003In twenty minutes\004 the ground was noticeably white.","The Silver Chair","C.S. Lewis"},
["22:21"]={"On a Saturday c. \0032221h\004., Lenz found a miniature bird that had fallen out of some nest and was sitting bald and pencil-necked on the lawn of Unit #3 flapping ineffectually.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["22:22"]={"It was now just \003twenty-two minutes past ten\004. They had been absent from the platoon for less than half an hour but, with the inferno raging at the company stores, both men were keenly aware that they had to get back to their men without delay.","Darkest Hour","James Holland"},
["22:23"]={"The mask leered at him out of a dark case. He hurried on to the next station, where he turned a key in a box. The box recorded the time: \00310:23 P.M.\004","Relic","Douglas Preston and Lincoln Child"},
["22:24"]={"Thanks to ten minutes or so of balmy weather, by \00310:24\004 the Earth is covered in the great carboniferous forests whose residues give us all our coal, and the first winged insects are evident.","A Short History of Nearly Everything","Bill Bryson"},
["22:25"]={"Mrs. Bultitaft always puts on the hot milk at ten. At about \003twenty-five minutes after\004 we saw Sally carrying her mug up to her room.","Cover Her Face","P.D. James"},
["22:26"]={"Siddons shuffled through some papers before he found the document he was looking for. He looked up at the judge and said, “I can confirm, sir, that the death certificate was signed at \003ten twenty-six p.m.\004 on Thursday the twenty-sixth of July, 1951.”","Best Kept Secret","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:27"]={"Mr. Harcourt woke up with mysterious suddenness at \003twenty-seven minutes past 10\004, and, by a curious coincidence, it was at that very instant that the butler came in with two footmen laden with trays of whisky, brandy, syphons, glasses and biscuits.","England, Their England","A.G. Macdonell"},
["22:28"]={"At \003twenty-eight minutes past ten\004, Florence began to wonder if those crackers were worth a reprimand from the Senior Control Committee.","Hail, California!","Mary E. Oliver"},
["22:30"]={"The time was \003ten-thirty\004 but it could have been three in the morning, because along its borders, West Berlin goes to bed with the dark","Smiley’s People","John le Carré"},
["22:31"]={"\00310:31 p.m.\004 OK. OK. Calm. Penny Husbands-Bosworth’s asbestos leukemia item is not on yet.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["22:32"]={"It was \003ten thirty-two\004 when the bus finally rolled into view.\nThe bus that came was a new type, not like the one I used to take to high school.","Blind Willow, Sleeping Woman","Haruki Murakami"},
["22:33"]={"He looked at his watch: \00310:33\004. He remembered being told, he couldn’t recall when or by whom, that it was her practice to take her nightly swim shortly after nine o’clock.","Devices and Desires","P.D. James"},
["22:34"]={"If you please. You went to bed at what time, Madame?\n“\003Just after half past ten.\004”","Death on the Nile","Agatha Christie"},
["22:35"]={"“What time does the concert end?” he asked the first uniformed official he spotted.\n“\003Ten thirty-five\004, sir, but you can’t leave your car there.”","As the Crow Flies","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:36"]={"Our take-off time was \00322:36\004 and as I lifted the heavy plane into the starlit night my hands and stomach felt as cold as ice.","Air Bridge","Hammond Innes"},
["22:37"]={"At \00310:37 p.m.\004 that night a fireball rips through Obscurity, killing Cripps but not before he’s called Goldilocks and left a message about something being ‘full of holes.’","The Fourth Bear","Jasper Fforde"},
["22:38"]={"Just a click as someone hung up the phone. It had been left at \00322:38\004 the previous evening. Jack didn’t have much doubt that it was someone checking to see if he was in.","The Kill Zone","Chris Ryan"},
["22:39"]={"Sunday, April 5\n\00310:39 P.M.\004\n“I didn’t know if I should have brought a bodyguard” he was saying as he strode in the door, a Master of the Universe with a leather jacket slung over his shoulder.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["22:40"]={"She climbed into bed at \00310:40\004, but couldn’t sleep for more than an hour at a time. She occasionally flicked on the television to watch spaghetti Westerns dubbed into Lebanese.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:41"]={"William listened to a debate on the future of Trident between Tony Blair and Michael Heseltine—both regarded as potential future leaders of their respective parties—when the lights went out in Summers’s living room at \00310:41\004. He turned the radio off and made another entry in his notebook.","Turn a Blind Eye","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:42"]={"We have established the exact time that Janisohn fell to the stage, the knife in his neck. It was \003eighteen minutes to eleven\004.","West of Guam: The Complete Cases of Jo Gar","Raoul Whitfield"},
["22:43"]={"Sebastian checked his watch: \00310:43 p.m.\004 “Then let’s go and find out if he’s still awake.”","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["22:44"]={"Alec pricked up his ears. “When was that?”\n“Oh, yesterday evening.”\n“What time?”\n“\003About a quarter to eleven\004. I was playing bridge.”","Dead in the Water","Carola Dunn"},
["22:45"]={"\00310:45 p.m.\004 Oh God. Daniel fell about laughing when I said I could not program video. Said he would do it for me. Still, at least I have done best for Mum. It is exciting and historic when one’s friends are on TV.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["22:46"]={"The ‘night train’ tallied to perfection, for high tide in the creek would be, as Davies estimated, between 10:30 and 11:00 p.m. on the night of the 25th; and the time-table showed that the only night train arriving at Norden was one from the south at \00310:46 p.m.\004","The Riddle of the Sands","Erskine Childers"},
["22:47"]={"On my screen the remaining theatregoers slowly drift away and when the timestamp clicks over to \00310:47 pm\004 there is no one left.","The Dark Lake","Sarah Bailey"},
["22:48"]={"Oh! I don’t know about that, said Mr. Satterthwaite, warming to his subject. “I was down there for a bit last summer. I found it quite convenient for town. Of course the trains only go every hour. 48 minutes past the hour from Waterloo-up to \00310:48\004.”","The Sign in the Sky","Agatha Christie"},
["22:49"]={"It’s \003well after 2245h\004. The dog’s leash slides hissing to the end of the Day-Glo line and stops the dog a couple of paces from the inside of the gate, where Lenz is standing, inclined in the slight forward way of somebody who’s talking baby-talk to a dog.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["22:50"]={"\00310:50 P. M.\004 This diary-keeping of mine is, I fancy, the outcome of that scientific habit of mind about which I wrote this morning. I like to register impressions while they are fresh.","The Parasite","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["22:51"]={"At \003nine minutes to eleven\004 the door of the house across the road opened. I knelt up in bed and peered out the window. It was Frau Gustavsen; she was walking across the drive with a garbage bag in her hand.","My Struggle: Book 1","Karl Ove Knausgaard"},
["22:52"]={"Now the player’s fever was in Rawley’s eyes. His face was deadly pale, but his hand threw steadily, calmly, almost negligently, as it might seem. All at once, at \003eight minutes to eleven\004, the luck turned in his favour, and his pile mounted again.","Northern Lights","Gilbert Parker"},
["22:53"]={"Every time I was there I saw you sitting at the end of the bar all by yourself, hunched over a cup of coffee. And every night at exactly \003seven minutes to eleven\004 you threw money on the bar, grabbed your coat, and headed out the door as fast as you were able.","All There Is","Kelly Krieg-Sigman with Dave Isay"},
["22:54"]={"They had a listing for Ozgard, Ramsey G., in the city. It was \00310:54\004 in Colorado, but the hour might make the call seem more urgent and therefore more credible.","Velocity","Dean Koontz"},
["22:55"]={"At \00310:55\004 they would enter the Farholme Gate, emerging a mere ten and a half minutes later at Bannermere Gate. Forty light-years away.","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["22:56"]={"It was \003about eleven o’clock\004. The stars were shining. The wind blew softly and carried the scent of decaying leaves and melting snow from the fields.","The Hammer of God","Bo Giertz"},
["22:57"]={"Then it grew dark; she would have had them to bed, but they begged sadly to be allowed to stay up; and, \003just about eleven o’clock\004, the door-latch was raised quietly, and in stepped the master.","Wuthering Heights","Emily Brontë"},
["22:58"]={"So when are they going?\n“Sunday night. I’m driving them down to Norwich to catch the eight-thirty, getting into Liverpool Street at \003ten-fifty-eight\004. Their daughter will meet them.”","Devices and Desires","P.D. James"},
["22:59"]={"They parked the car outside Lowther’s at precisely \003one minute to eleven\004. People were leaving, not all of them happy at having their evening curtailed. But the grumbling was muted, and even then it only started once they were safely on the street.","The Complaints","Ian Rankin"},
